# Per-package license grants.
#
# make.conf sets ACCEPT_LICENSE="-* @FREE @BINARY-REDISTRIBUTABLE", which is
# the right default: nothing proprietary installs unless it is named here.
# The alternative — widening make.conf to @EULA or "*" — would silently accept
# every future proprietary dependency anything ever pulls in, and there would
# be no record of which ones you had actually agreed to. This file is that
# record: one line per program, and a `git log` on it is the audit trail.
#
# Everything below is a proprietary binary repack installed by the `apps`
# phase (phases/25-apps.sh). media-video/obs-studio is absent on purpose —
# it is GPL-2 and needs no grant.

app-office/obsidian Obsidian-EULA
gui-apps/1password all-rights-reserved
app-misc/1password-cli all-rights-reserved
net-im/slack all-rights-reserved
